  "title": "Entity Framework Core Change Tracking",
  "description": "Deep dive into change tracking with DebugView and explicit tracking methods.",
  "order": 2,
  "difficulty": "intermediate",
  "estimatedMinutes": 35,
  "tags": ["ef-core", "change-tracking", "debugview", "explicit-tracking"],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "EF Core Change Tracker keeps track of all loaded entities and applies changes to the database when SaveChanges is called."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Tracking Conditions"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Entities are tracked when:"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "Returned from a query executed on the database",
          "Attached to DbContext by Add, Attach, Update methods",
          "A new entity connected to an existing tracked entity"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Stop Tracking Conditions"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": ["The entity is detached", "DbContext is disposed", "Change Tracker is cleared"]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "ChangeTracker.DebugView"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Use `DebugView.LongView` to see detailed information about tracked entities:"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "data": {
        "title": "DebugView Example",
        "content": "Using ChangeTracker.DebugView for debugging",
        "language": "csharp",
        "code": "var dept = context.Department.Include(e => e.Employees)\n    .First(e => e.Name == \"Development\");\n\ndept.Name = \".NET Development\";\n\ncontext.ChangeTracker.DetectChanges();\nConsole.WriteLine(context.ChangeTracker.DebugView.LongView);"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Explicit Tracking Methods"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "data": {
        "headers": ["Method", "State", "Description"],
        "rows": [
          ["Add", "Added", "Insert new entity"],
          ["Attach", "Unchanged", "Start tracking existing entity"],
          ["Update", "Modified", "Mark entity as modified"],
          ["Remove", "Deleted", "Mark entity for deletion"]
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Navigation Changes"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Relationships can be changed by:"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "Changing Collection Navigations (parent.Employees.Add/Remove)",
          "Changing Reference Navigations (employee.Department = newDept)",
          "Changing Foreign Key Values (employee.DepartmentId = newId)"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Principal Entity Deletion"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Deleting a principal entity affects dependents based on relationship type:"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "**Required Relationship** - Child entities are also deleted",
          "**Optional Relationship** - Child FK values set to null"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "summary-box",
      "data": {
        "title": "Key Takeaways",
        "points": [
          "DebugView provides detailed tracking information",
          "Add/Attach/Update/Remove for explicit tracking",
          "Navigation changes update relationships automatically",
          "Principal deletion behavior depends on relationship type"
        ],
        "takeaway": "Continue to learn about TrackGraph for entity graphs."
      }
    }
  ],
